banana mark can you guess which outer  banks star liked to venture off into the  wilderness on set  outer banks has become quite the  surprise hit with the first two seasons  topping the netflix charts  it seems like the show's breakout stars  had just as much fun filming the first  two seasons as we did watching them  so break out your surfboards as we dive  into some of the behind the scenes fun  of outer banks that's sarah cameron coop  princess  madeline klein has proved to be the  breakout star of outer banks as john b's  girlfriend and kooks princess  sarah cameron despite her stunning looks  according to klein's co-star madison  bailey  she's much funnier than one would expect  maddie  is just goofy she is just  plain silly bailey went on to gush over  klein's sense of humor  claiming that beneath her model-like  exterior she's just a silly dork on the  inside  she's has a very silly sense of humor  it seems like rudy ponco shares much  more in common with his character jj  than you might expect  madison bailey revealed that panko lives  like he's in an outer banks episode  every waking hour of the day rudy bonko  is an adventure boy something people may  not know is that  in between takes he will often go  explore  things in the woods ponco's co-stars  claim that whenever they're filming  outside he would be climbing trees or  searching for hidden treasure  much like jj despite being the oldest  member of the show's young cast  chase stokes sure likes to clown around  on set when he's not turning on the  charm as teen hero jon b  rudy ponco definitely has some funny and  fond memories of working with stokes  whenever chase is on set and i'm with  him he's usually following some prop  trying and making a joke out of it panko  claims that most of the bloopers from  the series have come from stokes goofing  off on camera  well if stokes and klein are both  goofballs  that must make them a match made in  heaven rudy ponco's claim that jonathan  davis's favorite place on set  when not on camera as the brainy pope  was the craft services table  honestly who could blame him if i could  just go do crap  jd's there picking the fruit snacks and  being like is there anything you know  sprouting  it's almost as if he eats one fruit  snack at a time and then goes back and  grabs another  i think we can all relate rudy ponco has  some great memories of madison bailey  who plays kai  on set for the first two seasons of the  show bayley actually liked to give her  fellow cast and crew some musical  entertainment between takes with her  ukulele skills  bailey if she doesn't have the ukulele  on set she probably like would check her  phone  and then she would then be hashing it  out with like  all of us on set bailey's co-stars  claimed that bayley was so  social that it felt like she was always  talking to somebody on set  while filming season one of the series  nobody on set predicted that season two  would actually happen  so reuniting for season two was a joyous  experience  the feeling of being all back together  was unreal  i mean it was like the instant same  connection as  season one i can't even describe it to  you you'll see it you know  you'll see that way on the screen stokes  went on to call the experience of  reuniting with his co-stars  a dream circumstance oftentimes the  chemistry between two performers can be  so undeniably strong  that it blossoms into real romance that  was the case with madeleine klein and  chase stokes who became an official  couple after filming the first season of  the show  it was just always work oriented for i  mean really till the day we wrapped  stokes says that his relationship with  klein really blossomed while  quarantining with her  despite their relationship stokes claims  that he and klein were able to find a  balance between business and pleasure  we did a good job of like not really  wanting to  though let's be honest for a second  sparks were definitely flying between  them on set as well  jonathan davis recalls that his first  scene he shot with madison bailey on  season two proved to be difficult for  both of them  despite it being an only dialogue driven  scene i went up to an auntie bailey i  just want to let you know that if you  had the call line i sure would have  because my line was right after years  and i had no idea what i was supposed to  say  there's nothing quite like the first day  jitters we're not storing a jail it's  not happening  i'm gonna see what i can do even if i  have to do it by myself one of panko's  absolute favorite moments while on set  for season two was filming the sequence  where jj attempts to break john b out of  jail  operation liberation baby oh boy let's  go  poncho recalls working with director  valerie weiss on the scene that takes  place in the fifth episode  the darkest hour weiss allowed ponco to  help decide on what jj would do during  the scene  telling him that if anything didn't work  she'd tweak it later in the end  weiss never found herself having to  touch up the scene leading to one of the  most memorable moments of the second  season  that was a fun experience i also had a  great time working with chase in that  scene  yeah that was that was a fun one as we  all know the cast of outer banks needed  to stay  fit and active for their roles  especially since their characters are  the definition of outdoorsmen  chase stokes and madeleine klein had to  endure some rigorous workout routines  from treadmills to kickboxing and  swimming in order to have the proper  physique for their characters  i started working out a lot stokes's  personal trainer is alex fine  who actually works with much of the cast  of riverdale  the mail stars on the set of obx season  2 had a rule amongst themselves  commit 100 to the fight scenes in order  to make them look as authentic as  possible  at one point jonathan davis was so  committed to a fight that he  accidentally clipped after drew starkey  who plays rafe  ouch  one of the most interesting aspects of  obx that helps it stand out from other  teen centric shows  is the fact that the cast looks much  more natural rather than the glamorous  aesthetic of the cast  of shows like gossip girl and riverdale  that's because the creative team wanted  the series leads to look sun-kissed and  tanned  that would fit in with the series  southern east coast setting i think  that's just what makes this show so  special  madeleine klein a natural brunette  wasn't too thrilled when she was told  that she had to dye her hair blonde  i had to get really real with myself and  be like do you want to do this  though by the time season 2 came around  klein had taken a liking to her golden  locks that's uh  that's the story of me being blonde for  outer banks  the young cast of outer banks sure  seemed to enjoy their time on set  especially judging from their social  media posts  klein posted a video from the filming of  season 2 where she records  chase stokes madison bailey jonathan  davis and rudy ponco who are  all seen driving in john b's van singing  alt j's indie hit  left hand free this is actually a direct  callback to the opening scene in season  one  the outer banks paradise on earth  nobody on the set of outer banks  expected the series to take off as much  as it did  which meant that there was an immense  amount of pressure felt by the cast and  creative team when season two rolled  around  compared to how they felt while filming  season one and then this year it was a  little different because there were eyes  on it and so i think i definitely put  pressure on myself  at the same time it's still just fun  over the course of filming both seasons  jonathan davis and rudy ponco have  become extremely close  to the point where they've both said  that even without knowing the future of  the show  they still plan on being close friends i  remember saying i would hang out with  this dude  despite anything with the show in fact  some of jd and rudy's banter on set was  recorded without them  even knowing and sometimes it would even  make it into the show  and then we would go back and watch the  show like holy crap like  that's in there now that is chemistry  when we were shooting we just kind of  focused on having fun it truly seems  like the cast of outer banks have formed  a tight-knit bond over the course of  filming the two seasons  from athletic training to improv and  even making true friendships  it makes us happy to know that the cast  of outer banks truly had a blast making  a show we love  what was your favorite moment in season  two
 

